      "enAnswer": "(1) If time permits, ask the travel agency to make a change;\n(2) If it cannot be arranged, the tour guide should patiently explain, clearly inform that the tickets have been booked and cannot be refunded or exchanged, and ask for their understanding. If these tourists insist on watching the Peking Opera, the tour guide should assist them in refunding the tickets, but the expenses shall be borne by themselves;\n(3) Discuss with the driver. If it is on the way, try to provide convenience for the minority of tourists; if it is in a different direction, coordinate and arrange transportation for them, but the expenses shall be borne by themselves.",
