      "question": "How should the tour guide respond when encountering continuous high temperature during the trip?",
      "answer": "(1) Report to the travel agency in a timely manner, reasonably adjust the itinerary, and reduce the group's outdoor activities during the high-temperature period;\n(2) Remind the group members to drink more water, eat small and frequent meals, and appropriately eat more bitter and acidic foods;\n(3) Remind the group members to avoid strenuous exercise, and can rinse their wrists with cold water or take a warm bath;\n(4) Remind the group members to take an appropriate nap during the day to replenish their physical strength;\n(5) Remind the group members to pay attention to sun protection and carry sun umbrellas, sun hats, etc., to prevent heatstroke.",
