      "enQuestion": "How should the tour guide respond if a sudden strong earthquake occurs after the group checks into the hotel?",
      "cnQuestion": "导游人员带团在酒店入住后遇到突发强震，应该如何应对？",
      "question": "How should the tour guide respond if a sudden strong earthquake occurs after the group checks into the hotel?",
      "answer": "(1) The tour guide should stay calm, comfort the group members, and organize the group members to transfer to the first floor of the hotel at the first time;\n(2) If the escape route is blocked, let the group members choose the triangular space indoors or the space with many pipelines to take shelter, and protect their heads;\n(3) Remind the tourists not to jump off the building or take the elevator to escape;\n(4) Send relevant distress information in a timely manner and strive to open up an escape route;\n(5) If it is temporarily impossible to escape, save physical strength, prevent suffocation, and wait for rescue.",
      "enAnswer": "(1) The tour guide should stay calm, comfort the group members, and organize the group members to transfer to the first floor of the hotel at the first time;\n(2) If the escape route is blocked, let the group members choose the triangular space indoors or the space with many pipelines to take shelter, and protect their heads;\n(3) Remind the tourists not to jump off the building or take the elevator to escape;\n(4) Send relevant distress information in a timely manner and strive to open up an escape route;\n(5) If it is temporarily impossible to escape, save physical strength, prevent suffocation, and wait for rescue.",
      "cnAnswer": "（1）导游员应沉着冷静，安慰团员，第一时间组织团员向酒店底楼转移；\n（2）如逃生通道阻塞，应让团员选择室内三角形空间或管道多的空间躲避，并保护好头部；\n（3）提醒游客切勿跳楼或乘坐电梯逃生；\n（4）及时发出相关求救信息，努力开辟逃生通道；\n（5）如暂时不能逃生则应保存体力，防止窒息，等待救援。"
