      "cnQuestion": "导游人员带团乘坐内河游轮遇突发水运事故，船只倾覆，应如何应对？",
      "question": "How should the tour guide respond if a sudden water transportation accident occurs when leading the group to take an inland cruise ship and the ship capsizes?",
      "answer": "(1) The tour guide should stay calm, comfort the group members, send a distress signal at the first time, and organize the group members to escape using life-saving equipment;\n(2) If it is necessary to jump into the water to escape, remind the tourists to wear life jackets, throw more floating items such as empty wooden boxes, wooden boards, and foam, and jump into the water from the lower deck of the cabin;\n(3) After jumping into the water, let the group members move away from the sinking ship as soon as possible, let the group float together, do not take off their clothes, maintain physical strength and body temperature, and wait for rescue;\n(4) Count the number of group members in a timely manner.",
      "enAnswer": "(1) The tour guide should stay calm, comfort the group members, send a distress signal at the first time, and organize the group members to escape using life-saving equipment;\n(2) If it is necessary to jump into the water to escape, remind the tourists to wear life jackets, throw more floating items such as empty wooden boxes, wooden boards, and foam, and jump into the water from the lower deck of the cabin;\n(3) After jumping into the water, let the group members move away from the sinking ship as soon as possible, let the group float together, do not take off their clothes, maintain physical strength and body temperature, and wait for rescue;\n(4) Count the number of group members in a timely manner.",
