      "cnQuestion": "导游人员带团游览过程中突遇洪水袭来，应如何应对？",
      "question": "How should the tour guide respond if a sudden flood occurs during the group tour?",
      "answer": "(1) The tour guide should stay calm, gather the group members at the first time, and evacuate to the surrounding high places in an orderly manner;\n(2) Try to send a distress signal as soon as possible to seek rescue;\n(3) If any tourist falls into the water, call on the tourist to try to hold onto floating objects or tree trunks, and not get close to electric poles or high-voltage towers;\n(4) If the tourist bus enters a flooded area, pay attention that the water level should not exceed the car chassis. If feasible, remind the driver to drive to a high place against the current as soon as possible, and do not let the current impact the car body from the side.",
      "enAnswer": "(1) The tour guide should stay calm, gather the group members at the first time, and evacuate to the surrounding high places in an orderly manner;\n(2) Try to send a distress signal as soon as possible to seek rescue;\n(3) If any tourist falls into the water, call on the tourist to try to hold onto floating objects or tree trunks, and not get close to electric poles or high-voltage towers;\n(4) If the tourist bus enters a flooded area, pay attention that the water level should not exceed the car chassis. If feasible, remind the driver to drive to a high place against the current as soon as possible, and do not let the current impact the car body from the side.",
