      "question": "How should the tour guide respond if a sudden debris flow or landslide occurs when leading the group to visit a mountainous area?",
      "answer": "(1) The tour guide should stay calm, gather the group members to evacuate to the stable areas on both sides, and do not evacuate along the mountain upwards or downwards;\n(2) The group should not take shelter under the hillside with falling rocks or a lot of accumulations;\n(3) The group should not stay in low-lying areas or climb trees to take shelter;\n(4) If the house where they are located is exactly in the landslide zone, try to quickly evacuate from the house to an open area;\n(5) Try to send a distress signal as soon as possible to seek rescue.",
